From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:11:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(webmock): replay JSON-RPC answers with the live id; key
 JSON-RPC calls by method

Copilot's replay miss was ours. It runs two tools/list calls to GitHub's
remote MCP at once (ids 1 and 2); both keyed exact, but the replayed answer
carried the recorded id 1, so call 2 timed out (60 s, three times), and the
cancel/retry calls fell to a loose key every MCP call shared, getting the
initialize answer. Copilot then sent 19 tools instead of 25 and every
/v1/messages call missed.

A replayed JSON-RPC answer now carries the live request's id (top-level
"id" of a JSON body or of each SSE data line), and a JSON-RPC body's method
is part of its loose key; no other loose key changes. Same copilot cell,
pre-scrub cassettes, Rust server: rc 1 in 152 s, 6 misses, 19 tools before;
rc 0 in 1 s, all exact, 25 tools, the recorded reply after. Committed
cassettes still miss on their <scratch> paths (declared, qualifier concern).
